<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">The Communist Manifesto</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1848">1848</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Communist Manifesto, Manifesto of the Communist Party</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Communist Manifesto, originally the Manifesto of the Communist Party, is a political pamphlet by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karl-marx">Karl Marx</a> and Friedrich Engels, commissioned by the Communist League and published anonymously in German in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> in February 1848. It argues that &quot;the history of all hitherto existing society is the history of class struggles&quot; and predicts that the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/proletariat">proletariat</a> will overthrow the bourgeoisie and bring about a classless society. It fell into obscurity after the defeat of the revolutions of 1848, revived in the 1870s and has become one of the world's most influential political documents.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/the-communist-manifesto.jpg" alt="The Communist Manifesto" width="320" height="501" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Friedrich Engels, Karl Marx · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Communist-manifesto.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
